===== _project/DONE/results-explorer-followup-todo-review/planning/results-explorer-result-detail-metric-formatting-regression.yaml =====

====================================================================================================
Restore Result Detail metric-formatting precision and unit contract after shared formatter rollout
====================================================================================================

Priority:  Critical
Status:    Completed
Worktree:  results-explorer-followup-todo-review
Category:  User Experience
File:      _project/DONE/results-explorer-followup-todo-review/planning/results-explorer-result-detail-metric-formatting-regression.yaml

Description:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The follow-up remediation release gate caught a post-merge regression in the
full Results Explorer frontend suite. `ResultDetail.test.tsx` now fails after
the shared metric-formatting rollout because the canonical result summary no
longer exposes exact power-score precision, and the median/raw duration table
contract no longer matches the rendered labels.

This is a release-blocking evidence issue, not just stale tests: Result
Detail is the route where users inspect an individual benchmark receipt, so
compact leaderboard/table formatting must not erase exact score evidence or
make raw timing units ambiguous.


Implementation Guardrails:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Must Preserve:
    - Leaderboard, benchmark, platform, query, and compare surfaces must keep compact large power-score formatting.
    - Result Detail must preserve exact score evidence for receipt-level inspection.
    - Timing headers must match the rendered timing unit contract.
    - Raw sort/comparison values must remain numeric and unrounded.

  Approach:
    Treat Result Detail as a detail/receipt surface, not a dense leaderboard
    surface. Preserve compact shared formatting where it improves scanning, but
    expose exact power-score evidence where users inspect a single result.

  Anti-Patterns:
    - DO NOT globally revert `fmtScore` to exact formatting.
    - DO NOT silence the failing tests without deciding the detail-route contract.
    - DO NOT add source changes outside Result Detail, shared formatter helpers, or focused tests unless reproduction proves the issue is shared.

  Verification:
    - Result Detail formatter regression tests pass
      Command: cd results-explorer && npm test -- --run src/pages/__tests__/ResultDetail.test.tsx
      Expected: ResultDetail tests pass
    - Full Results Explorer frontend suite passes
      Command: cd results-explorer && npm test -- --run
      Expected: all frontend tests pass
    - Typecheck and build pass
      Command: cd results-explorer && npm run typecheck && npm run build
      Expected: both commands exit 0

  Scope Limit:
    Only modify:
      - results-explorer/src/pages/ResultDetail.tsx
      - results-explorer/src/pages/__tests__/ResultDetail.test.tsx
      - results-explorer/src/lib/metricFormatters.ts
      - results-explorer/src/lib/__tests__/metricFormatters.test.ts
      - results-explorer/src/utils.ts
      - results-explorer/src/__tests__/utils.test.ts
